---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The plan that verifies one finished run's follow-ups through onefollowup: prepare the batch,
  have the verifying agent dispose every draft and input, check, publish and settle. `just
  follow-ups` creates it, and `scripts/run-ended.sh` through that recipe.
variables:
  project:
    description: The plan's native id, which every member's own id is prefixed with.
    type: string
    required: true
  run:
    description: The run whose follow-ups this plan verifies, as the engine names it.
    type: string
    required: true
  batch:
    description: The onefollowup batch, which is the run's public id.
    type: string
    required: true
  checkout:
    description: The absolute path of the checkout the plan is launched from, where every onefollowup command runs.
    type: string
    required: true
  store:
    description: The absolute directory of the onetaskgraph store onefollowup works beside.
    type: string
    required: true
  task_loader:
    description: The loader document `onepipeline template resolve follow-up-task --json` stated, which the verifying agent's task is rendered through.
    type: string
    required: true
members:
  - id: "{{ project }}-prepare"
    title: "Prepare the follow-up batch {{ batch }}"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Snapshot the batch's drafts and budget inputs, read the destination, and write the verifying agent's task."}
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: prepare
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [onefollowup, prepare, --batch, "{{ batch }}"]
  - id: "{{ project }}-verify"
    title: "Verify the follow-ups of run {{ run }}"
    template: {loader: "{{ task_loader }}"}
    answers:
      mode: initial
      batch: "{{ batch }}"
      checkout: "{{ checkout }}"
      task_file: "{{ store }}/.onefollowup/tasks/{{ batch }}/task.md"
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-prepare"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: verify
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/follow-up.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/follow-up.yaml
  - id: "{{ project }}-check"
    title: "Check the follow-up batch {{ batch }}"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Hold the batch's dispositions, tickets and staged writes to onefollowup's rules before anything is written."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-verify"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: check
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [onefollowup, check, --batch, "{{ batch }}"]
  - id: "{{ project }}-publish"
    title: "Publish the follow-up batch {{ batch }}"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Send the batch's staged writes to the destination and receipt every outcome."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-check"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: publish
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [onefollowup, publish, --batch, "{{ batch }}"]
  - id: "{{ project }}-settle"
    title: "Settle the follow-up batch {{ batch }}"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Read back what no answer confirmed, raise the follow-up review, and retire the batch's working files."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-publish"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: settle
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [onefollowup, settle, --batch, "{{ batch }}"]
---
Verify the follow-up drafts and budget inputs run `{{ run }}` left, through onefollowup, and
put the verified tickets on the destination `onefollowup.yaml` names.
